2026-09-07 08:51:24 - basic/data_engineer - INFO - {'otrace': ['medallion_governance_auditor'], 'text': 'result from lakehouse_quality_specialist\n# Bronze to Silver Data Processing\n\n## Raw Payload Analysis\n```python\n# Input: JSON string with user record\nraw_payload = "{{\'user_id\': \'USR-8821\', \'full_name\': \'Jane Doe\', \'email\': \'jane.doe@example.com\', \'ssn\': \'999-00-1234\', \'signup_timestamp\': \'2026-09-07T14:20:00Z\', \'city\': \'Austin\', \'status\': \'ACTIVE\'}}"\n```\n\n## PySpark Bronze → Silver Transformation\n\n```python\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession\nfrom pyspark.sql.functions import col, to_timestamp, when, trim, sha2, concat\nfrom pyspark.sql.types import StructType, StructField, StringType, TimestampType\n\nspark = SparkSession.builder.getOrCreate()\n\n# Define schema for memory efficiency\nschema = StructType([\n    StructField("user_id", StringType(), False),\n    StructField("full_name", StringType(), True),\n    StructField("email", StringType(), True),\n    StructField("ssn", StringType(), True),\n    StructField("signup_timestamp", StringType(), True),\n    StructField("city", StringType(), True),\n    StructField("status", StringType(), True)\n])\n\n# Parse raw JSON payload\ndf_raw = spark.read.json(spark.sparkContext.parallelize([raw_payload]), schema=schema)\n\n# Bronze to Silver transformation\ndf_silver = (\n    df_raw\n    # Trim string fields\n    .withColumn("user_id", trim(col("user_id")))\n    .withColumn("full_name", trim(col("full_name")))\n    .withColumn("email", trim(col("email")))\n    .withColumn("city", trim(col("city")))\n    # Cast timestamp\n    .withColumn("signup_timestamp", to_timestamp(col("signup_timestamp"), "yyyy-MM-dd\'T\'HH:mm:ss\'Z\'"))\n    # Hash PII fields (SSN masked at Silver)\n    .withColumn("ssn_hash", sha2(concat(col("ssn"), col("user_id")), 256))\n    .drop("ssn")\n    # Null handling\n    .fillna({\n        "full_name": "UNKNOWN",\n        "email": "unknown@unknown.com",\n        "city": "UNKNOWN",\n        "status": "PENDING"\n    })\n    # Validate status\n    .withColumn("status", \n        when(col("status").isin("ACTIVE", "INACTIVE", "SUSPENDED"), col("status"))\n        .otherwise("UNKNOWN")\n    )\n    # Deduplication key\n    .withColumn("dedup_key", col("user_id"))\n)\n\n# Show result\ndf_silver.display()\n```\n\n## Output Schema (Silver Layer)\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `user_id` | string | Primary key, trimmed |\n| `full_name` | string | Nulls filled with "UNKNOWN" |\n| `email` | string | Nulls filled with placeholder |\n| `city` | string | Nulls filled with "UNKNOWN" |\n| `status` | string | Validated enum |\n| `signup_timestamp` | timestamp | ISO 8601 parsed |\n| `ssn_hash` | string | SHA-256 hashed (PII masked) |\n| `dedup_key` | string | For deduplication watermark |\n\n## Key Optimizations Applied\n- ✅ Schema defined upfront (avoids schema inference)\n- ✅ PII (SSN) hashed, not stored in clear text\n- ✅ Timestamp properly cast to `TimestampType`\n- ✅ Null handling with sensible defaults\n- ✅ Deduplication key added for downstream processing'}
